   "note": "New ALMA Band 3 (3mm) observation of MP Mus (PDS 66), a different band/config from the existing exoALMA Band 7 (0.9mm) record. The 3mm data reveal a ring at 10.5au and gaps at 7.5/15au that are undetected at 0.9/1.3mm, plus hints of an inner cavity (<3au). The paper infers a hidden gas-giant companion (1-3 au) from the disk structure plus a Gaia astrometric proper-motion anomaly and hydrodynamic simulations -- the planet is NOT directly imaged, so per instructions it was NOT added to planets[] with method imaging; recommend adding a system-notes line instead, e.g.: 'Gaia astrometry + ALMA 3mm ring/cavity structure (Ribas et al. 2025) indicate an unseen ~1-3 au gas-giant companion; not directly imaged.'"
